.TH XWOB-SETTINGS 1 "2026" "xwob" "xwob Manual"
.SH NAME
xwob-settings \- graphical settings for the xwob overlay bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xwob-settings
[\fB\-c\fR \fIfile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Edits the one configuration file read by both xwob backends (X11 and Wayland),
.I ~/.config/xwob/xwob.ini
by default. Layout, colours (with transparency) and behaviour are on three
tabs.
.PP
.B Live
shows the bar with the settings currently in the window, saved or not, on a
temporary copy of the configuration. The slider and the
.B Alt
box choose what value is shown.
.PP
.B Apply
writes the file and runs
.BR "xwob \-\-reload" ,
so bars that are already running pick up the new settings at once; no
logout or restart is needed. Unknown keys and Wayland-only sections
(\fB[output.*]\fR, extra \fB[style.*]\fR) already in the file are kept, but
comments next to the keys the window edits are not.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIfile\fR
Edit this file instead of the default.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XWOB_BIN
The xwob launcher used for preview and reload (default: the one next to
xwob-settings, then PATH).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xwob (1)
